window.docContents[52].resolve({"/Error-Functions___-Dawson___s-and-Fresnel-Integrals/#chapter-7":{"contents":"Source: NIST Digital Library of Mathematical Functions, Chapter 7.\n\n\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean","header":"7. Error Functions, Dawson's and Fresnel Integrals","id":"/Error-Functions___-Dawson___s-and-Fresnel-Integrals/#chapter-7"},"/Finite-error-bounds/#chapter-1":{"contents":"This chapter introduces only LMLF notation. General analysis already available in Mathlib is not\nrepeated.\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean","header":"1. Finite error bounds","id":"/Finite-error-bounds/#chapter-1"},"/Gamma-Function/Gamma-Function-Inequalities/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Gamma-Function--Gamma-Function-Inequalities--___5___6-Inequalities--___5___6_LPAR_i_RPAR_-Real-Variables--Kershaw___s-Inequality":{"contents":"For 0<s<1,\n\\exp\\!\\left((1-s)\\psi(x+\\sqrt{s})\\right)\n\\le \\frac{\\Gamma(x+1)}{\\Gamma(x+s)}\n\\le \\exp\\!\\left((1-s)\\psi\\!\\left(x+\\frac{s+1}{2}\\right)\\right).Kershaw's inequality gives two non-strict exponential bounds for the Gamma quotient. Mathlib has\na canonical complex digamma function but no separate real-valued name, so realDigamma restricts\nthat function to the real axis by taking its real part. Every digamma argument here is positive.\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Gamma Function\u0009Gamma-Function Inequalities\u0009§5.6 Inequalities\u0009§5.6(i) Real Variables","header":"Kershaw's Inequality","id":"/Gamma-Function/Gamma-Function-Inequalities/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Gamma-Function--Gamma-Function-Inequalities--___5___6-Inequalities--___5___6_LPAR_i_RPAR_-Real-Variables--Kershaw___s-Inequality"}});